{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>To her, as a maidservant.</b> There is a fine point to examine in the word <b>lah</b> ('to her'): to say that the maidservant was hers, as I explained in the verse (Genesis 29:24) ״וַיִּתֵּן לָבָן אֶת זִלְפָּה״." "<b>Or</b> it may intend that he stipulated with her that her husband would have no rights in her, along the lines of what Rambam wrote (Laws of Marriage, ch. 22): one who gives a gift to a woman on condition that her husband has no rights in it — the husband does not consume its produce. For everything that can be interpreted to Laban's discredit, we so interpret."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:53.518754897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}